    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-05-20 hinges on exploiting favorable matchups against secondary arms. **Kyle Tucker** (78.84) stands as the undeniable anchor of the lineup today, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against V\u00e1squez, where he leverages a significant SP skill boost (+19%) to secure the slate's highest efficiency score. He is complemented well by **Josh Jung** (64.09), who enjoys an aggressive park factor (+14%) against Freeland, and **Andy Pages** (64.84), who remains a high-floor play in the same favorable Vasquez matchup. Despite the scarcity of stolen bases, we are prioritizing **Josh Lowe** (62.74) and **Nasim Nunez** (60.49) despite their bottom-of-the-order placements; their sprint speed and matchup data provide the necessary leverage to keep us competitive in the SB category without sacrificing excessive production.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Liam Hicks**, who fell well below the 40.0 efficiency threshold. While **Liam Hicks** possesses latent potential, the combination of a daunting matchup against Sale (2.90 xERA) and a poor platoon split suppressed his score to 29.95, effectively disqualifying him from consideration. We continue to monitor the status of our core, as **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth options for high-leverage pivots. We are tracking lineups for **Gunnar Henderson**, who faces a stiff test against Matz; his 50.28 score is heavily penalized by a difficult platoon environment, making him a candidate for late-game substitution if his production lags behind **Sam Antonacci** (59.55) or **Nolan Schanuel** (58.78), who are both well-positioned to capitalize on the Civale matchup.",
